      "name": "Content Architecture & First Principles",
      "content": "**3.1 Executive Overview**\\nThe episode opens with a brief introduction, then moves into Elisa’s personal journey from audiovisual studies to language‑teaching, followed by a deep dive into routine‑building strategies for French learners. Core messages include the necessity of daily exposure, integrating language into existing habits, and avoiding the “one‑hour‑per‑week” trap. The host repeatedly emphasizes regular, low‑friction practice as the engine of progress.\\n\\n**3.2 First Principles Deconstruction**\\n- **Foundational Axiom**: Language acquisition is a cumulative skill that requires consistent input and output.\\n- **Irreducible Elements**: (1) Daily exposure, (2) Active production, (3) Feedback loop.\\n- **Reconstructed Logic**: Elisa maps these elements onto everyday routines (YouTube playlists, podcasts, phone language settings) to lower activation energy for practice.\\n- **Hidden Assumptions**: Learners have access to digital devices and are motivated to modify their environment.\\n\\n**3.3 Temporal Content Map & Arc Analysis**\\n| Segment | Approx. Position | Focus |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Intro & Guest Welcome | Start | Set context, announce training program |\\n| Personal Backstory | Early | Explain career shift, credibility |\\n| Routine Theory | Mid | Discuss regularity, habit stacking |\\n| Practical Tips | Later | Playlists, shadowing, speaking aloud |\\n| Closing Advice | End | Long‑term mindset, book recommendation |",
